orthoo-ai
=========

orthoo-ai is a standalone project. It is not published, endorsed or supported
by the project its code came from, and it shares none of that project's
servers, accounts, signing keys or store listings.


Origin of the code
------------------

The source derives from PocketPal AI 1.23.0 by Asghar Ghorbani, released under
the MIT License. That license requires its copyright and permission notice to
stay with copies of the software, so LICENSE keeps the line
"Copyright (c) 2024 Asghar Ghorbani" unchanged. If you want to claim your own
changes, add your own copyright line to LICENSE next to it; do not remove it.


Names and artwork
-----------------

The PocketPal name, logo and mascot artwork are not part of orthoo-ai: the
name, the launcher icons (Android and iOS), the splash mark and the in-app mark
were replaced with original artwork (see scripts/app-icon/). The MIT License
does not grant rights to another project's name or logos. A few inherited
in-app illustrations remain, for example the "Pip" character on the last
onboarding screen, and the screenshots in assets/ show the original app's
interface. Replace them if you want fully original artwork.


Pieces that still come from the original author's namespace
------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing in orthoo-ai needs the original project's servers, and no feature is
locked behind them. Two things still come from the original author's
namespace and are worth mirroring or replacing for full independence:

- npm packages @pocketpalai/react-native-speech and
  @pocketpalai/react-native-speech-phonon. They drive text-to-speech and are
  installed from the public npm registry under their own licenses
  (node_modules/<package>/LICENSE after `yarn install`, and the in-app
  "Open-source notices" screen).
- Hugging Face repositories under palshub/ (phonemizer-dicts,
  kitten-tts-nano-0.8-fp32, phonon-31m-en-coreml). Some voices download them
  on demand. They are public and carry their own licenses. Their locations are
  listed in src/services/tts/constants.ts.

Internal database names that still contain "palshub" (WatermelonDB tables and
the Pal.source field) are identifiers only. They make no network requests.


Other open-source components
----------------------------

llama.cpp, whisper.cpp, ONNX Runtime, React Native and the other libraries
listed in package.json are used under their own licenses. The in-app
"Open-source notices" screen lists the ones bundled with the app.
